 Prop name          | Type    | Required? | Description
-------------------------------------------------------------------
isOpen			      bool      yes         dictates whether modal is open or not
title                 string	yes			Title for the modal
size				  string    			optional, 3 sizes: large, medium, small; default small
text			      string				Text inside the modal
onCancel			  func		yes			function to close modal (most likely set modal show state in parent to false)
onOK				  func		yes			function to submit/proceed with an action
onOKtext			  string				[deprecated] Text that will appear on the onOK button
onCanceltext          string                [deprecated] Text that will appear on the onCancel button
isDeleteModal		  bool					if this is true, button will show a red "Delete"
doNotShowChecked      bool					boolean property to store checked/unchecked state in input checkbox
handleChange		  func					toggles checked property. Example use in parent: this.setState({[e.target.name]: etarget.checked})
name				  string				name to associate button IDs and checkbox reference
additionalClasses	  string				Additional classes added to the Modal wrapper
doNotShowAgainText    bool					if true, the "Do not show again" section will be displayed to user
onAfterOpen			  func                  function to perform action after modal is open (Like focus on any element)
button				  object				{
												okClass: class name to be use in OK button (default: btn-primary)
												okLabel: label for OK button (default: OK)
